---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"ipcrm\")"
---
Remove System V IPC resources.

Uses shmctl(2), msgctl(2), or semctl(2) with IPC_RMID to remove shared memory segments, message
queues, or semaphore arrays.

Usage: ipcrm [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -m, --shmem-id <SHMEM_ID>
          Remove shared memory segment by ID

  -M, --shmem-key <SHMEM_KEY>
          Remove shared memory segment by key

  -q, --queue-id <QUEUE_ID>
          Remove message queue by ID

  -Q, --queue-key <QUEUE_KEY>
          Remove message queue by key

  -s, --semaphore-id <SEMAPHORE_ID>
          Remove semaphore array by ID

  -S, --semaphore-key <SEMAPHORE_KEY>
          Remove semaphore array by key

  -a, --all [<ALL>]
          Remove all IPC resources (optionally: shm, msg, sem)

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
